{
 "schema": "sim-xp/playbook@2",
 "meta": {
  "id": "kafka-rebalance-storm",
  "title": "The rebalance storm: when slow looks dead",
  "story": "A payments team consumes an orders topic with three workers. A database migration makes each record slower to process. Nobody's consumer crashes, yet within minutes the group is stuck in a loop of rebalances and lag is climbing.",
  "duration_s": 420,
  "tags": [
   "kafka",
   "consumer-groups",
   "rebalancing",
   "backpressure"
  ],
  "background": [
   {
    "title": "The system",
    "body": "checkout-api publishes every order to a 6-partition orders topic. Three payments workers form one consumer group and charge the orders, each polling a batch of up to 500 records, processing them one by one against Postgres, then committing."
   },
   {
    "title": "How it normally works",
    "body": "A worker must call poll() again within max.poll.interval.ms (5 minutes). If it does not, the group coordinator decides it is dead, removes it, and rebalances: partitions are reassigned to whoever is left. Normally a batch takes seconds and this never comes up."
   },
   {
    "title": "Today",
    "body": "A database migration adds a fraud_score lookup with no index yet, which makes each record about 650 ms slower. Nothing crashes and nothing alerts."
   }
  ],
  "cast": [
   {
    "name": "checkout-api",
    "role": "produces about 1,200 orders a second"
   },
   {
    "name": "orders topic",
    "role": "6 partitions, two per worker"
   },
   {
    "name": "payments-worker-1, -2, -3",
    "role": "one consumer group, one batch each"
   },
   {
    "name": "payments-db",
    "role": "looked up for every record"
   }
  ],
  "watch": [
   {
    "label": "Consumer lag",
    "normal": "normal: near 0"
   },
   {
    "label": "Group rebalances",
    "normal": "normal: almost never"
   },
   {
    "label": "DB query p99",
    "normal": "normal: about 45 ms"
   }
  ],
  "learn": [
   "why a slow worker can look dead to Kafka",
   "why a rebalance makes the next one more likely",
   "how batch size, timeouts and rebalancing mode fit together"
  ],
  "layout": {
   "columns": 2,
   "rows": 4
  }
 },
